{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548271-contradiction-do-beasts-in-their-lair-merge-with-the-soul-or-not","id":548271,"title":"Contradiction: Do Beasts In Their Lair Merge With The Soul or Not?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-10T04:17:31-07:00","id":548271,"title":"Contradiction: Do Beasts In Their Lair Merge With The Soul or Not?","content":"Page 120 says that Beasts merge with their Soul when in their lair, but the fiction on page 329 describes the Beast and her Soul as separate. Which is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:45:02-07:00","id":548448,"title":"","content":"Within their lair, a beast merges with their soul <i>unless they are at satiety 10. </i>In that case, they remain separate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T05:46:42-07:00","id":551283,"title":"","content":"To let my Beast's explore Astral Realms with mages, I plan on house ruling things, so <b>Beast is always in his Souls form in Astral, apart of Astral Strata character is</b>. I think also about letting <b>Beast character to change his Dream Form to it's human body - and letting Soul return to Lair - by spending point of Satiety</b>. What do you think about those rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:51:59-07:00","id":551464,"title":"","content":"I'd say to ignore the fiction and go with the rules, as a general rule of thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:35:48-07:00","id":551573,"title":"","content":"I'd probably let the beast take on their souls appearance in the astral (especially when using atavisms) but keep the stats as their mental ones only. You're like, a projection. There's no fleshy shell to constrain you, but you're still not at full power. I'd probably let them switch between soul and human form appearance while they're merged in their lair too. But again, the stats wouldn't change (staying as full soul level this time) and they'd revert to beast form (at least partially, like growing claws or whatever) if they used any powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:48:18-07:00","id":551835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548271-contradiction-do-beasts-in-their-lair-merge-with-the-soul-or-not#post548271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 120 says that Beasts merge with their Soul when in their lair, but the fiction on page 329 describes the Beast and her Soul as separate. Which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah the Retreat fiction. That actually does have a mechanical representation, though its easy to miss. If the Beast hits satiety 10 the Soul goes into slumber, if the human part attempts to wake it up then they have to show up in the lair and the rules actually do state that the two don't merge at that time. Which leaves the fun situation of walking through whatever nightmarish and potentially lethal landscape your lair is without the your normal immunity to your own lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:19:27-07:00","id":556334,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I missed that... That really is a brilliantly cool thing, a character wandering through their Lair without immunity in their fleshy human form for once. Luckily getting Satiety 10 is fairly rare, if you balance your character's feeding correctly. Makes also a great opposite to Satiety 0 which can bring in lethal damage after time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:41:24-07:00","id":556351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/548271-contradiction-do-beasts-in-their-lair-merge-with-the-soul-or-not?p=556334#post556334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, I missed that... That really is a brilliantly cool thing, a character wandering through their Lair without immunity in their fleshy human form for once. Luckily getting Satiety 10 is fairly rare, if you balance your character's feeding correctly. Makes also a great opposite to Satiety 0 which can bring in lethal damage after time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I only found it because I had been wondering what the conditions were that woke a Beast from Slumber and that one seemed the least annoying/ potentially hazardous to your health. <br /> The others are destroying a chamber in the lair, or being injured almost to the point of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}